foreseer.explore-with-gaussian-gradient (bool)
  if gaussian gradient should be used in the exploring step, defaults to true

foreseer.explore-with-random (float)
  ratio of random extra gaussian should be picked in the exploring step, setting to 0 will disable this
  defaults to 0

foreseer.use-dldl (bool)
foreseer.use-dl1 (bool)
foreseer.use-dssim (bool)
  if certain metric should be used during decision making, defaults to true

foreseer.strict (bool)
  strict mode: gaussian must decrease on all metrics used during decision making to be selected
  defaults to false, which means decreasing on any metric used is sufficient for gaussian to be selected

foreseer.target-gaussian (int)
  number of gaussian to reach after all densify steps, defaults to 0 which means do not apply growth control
  if the number of gaussian proposed to be densified at any step exceeds the budget for that step, proposed
   gaussian will be sampled randomly weighted by their maximum decrease amongst all metrics used.
  See also foreseer.temperature-modifier, which will alter the behavior of this modification.
  this might be moved to global namespace since growth control is not limited to foreseer densify classifier.

foreseer.visualize-views (int)
  number of views to visualize. defaults to 0 which means visualization will be skipped.
  Since foreseer adjusts the iteration counter from time to time, it has to implement visualization separately
   to acquire correct result.

foreseer.temperature-modifier (float)
  each gaussian, given its reduced metric (minimum among all metrics if strict, minimum otherwise) m, the
   temperature modifier k, index of current densify step i and total number of densify steps t, has a
   probability p = 2 / 2 + exp(-k * (i / t) * m) of being selected as a candidate.
  Random sampling (introduced by foreseer.target-gaussian) is applied after this random candidate selection,
   and an uniformed (unweighted) sampling will be used instead of a weighted one.
  If the value supplied is 0 or negative, this modification is disabled. Defaults to 0.

foreseer.clustering (float)
  use clustering to include gaussians not explored but with similar features as explored gaussians that are
   decided to be densified into candidates
  The value indicates maximum distance between 2 feature points such they reside in the same neighborhood when
   clustering with DBSCAN. Distance between two feature points is defined as their euclidean distance. Each
   dimension in the feature is rescaled into range [0, 1].
  If 0 is specified, clustering will be disabled. Defaults to 0.

foreseer.neighbor-ratio (float)
  neighbor size ratio, setting to 0 disables this feature. Defaults to 0.

